From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:17:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: let fade steps ride on client presents

The fade between panel backlight levels was meant to ride on the
compositor's flips, and every client present does carry a pending level:
iomfb_m4_swap() calls dcp_backlight_prepare() for each present and sends
a dirty level with it. But each fade step kicks the backlight work at
once, and the work takes dcp->lock and sends a brightness-only present of
the active frame within microseconds, long before the client's next
present 8 ms later. That present then finds nothing pending. So every
step took a swap slot of its own: on a MacBook Pro (14-inch, M4) with the
ambient-light brightness service running, a 120 Hz vkmark run did about
12 brightness-only presents per brightness change (backlight_swaps +290
for 24 changes) and its client flips dropped by 5.5%, from 119 to 113
frames per second. With the service stopped and backlight_swaps flat,
the same runs gave 119 frames per second.

Leave a pending level to the client while it flips. The backlight work
sends a brightness-only present only once no client frame is due: the
client's own frame interval after its last present, bounded to one to
two vblanks, plus half a vblank. Until then it looks again at that time;
a client present in between carries the level and the work finds nothing
pending. Brightness-only presents are also at most one per vblank. The
vblank is the running mode's (PreferredTimingElements), 120 Hz until it
is known.

The fade's clock, its steps and its last level are unchanged; this only
picks the present that carries each step. With no client presents a
level goes out at once, as before, so a fade on an idle screen still ends
at its target when its 250 ms are up. debugfs iomfb_m4 gains
backlight_carried (client presents that carried a new level) and
backlight_deferred (brightness-only presents put off).

Add KUnit cases for the decision: a 120 Hz and a 60 Hz client, a stopped
client, the two-vblank bound and the one-per-vblank limit; a fade under a
120 Hz client that needs no brightness-only present and ends at its
target; and the same fade on an idle screen, which presents its target
between 250 and 300 ms.

Fixes: d434b638c87b ("drm/apple: m4: fade between panel backlight levels")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 312efefe283e195810bf1290d34414fab2f67261)
[k612 head: re-applied after the drm/apple file-level sync (e37e898874 rebased), which replaced
 dcp_backlight.h, dcp_backlight_test.c and iomfb_m4.c; same 3-file diff, +224/-6]
(cherry picked from commit 879a746127c85be3c18d5946e4fa90ca784418d5)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.h      |  25 ++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight_test.c | 137 +++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c           |  65 +++++++++-
 3 files changed, 221 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.h
index cc2d321fb1..e5bcd7028d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.h
@@ -368,6 +368,31 @@ static inline bool dcp_bl_swap_finish(struct dcp_backlight_state *state,
 			      swap->accepted && swap->completed);
 }
 
+/*
+ * A brightness-only present takes a swap slot of its own, while every client
+ * present already carries a pending level (dcp_bl_prepare() runs for each).
+ * So while a client flips, leave a fade step to its next present: send a
+ * brightness-only present only when no client frame is due, that is once the
+ * client's own frame interval after its last present, bounded to one to two
+ * vblanks, and half a vblank more have passed without one.  Brightness-only
+ * presents are also at most one per vblank.  Times are in ns, 0 before the
+ * first present of each kind.  Returns how long to wait; 0 sends it now.
+ */
+static inline u64 dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(u64 now, u64 last_flip, u64 flip_interval,
+				      u64 last_swap, u64 vblank)
+{
+	u64 due = 0;
+
+	if (!vblank)
+		return 0;
+	if (last_flip)
+		due = last_flip + clamp(flip_interval, vblank, 2 * vblank) +
+		      vblank / 2;
+	if (last_swap)
+		due = max(due, last_swap + vblank);
+	return due > now ? due - now : 0;
+}
+
 struct apple_dcp;
 
 void dcp_backlight_desktop_power(struct apple_dcp *dcp, bool on);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight_test.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight_test.c
index 9cbf111430..55e92a3b9f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight_test.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight_test.c
@@ -808,6 +808,143 @@ static void edr_timed_limits_test(struct kunit *test)
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dcp_edr_next_timed(15000, 16000, 16000, 60, 30, 8333), 16000U);
 }
 
+#define RIDE_VBLANK	8333333ULL	/* 120 Hz */
+#define RIDE_MS		1000000ULL
+
+static void backlight_ride_wait_test(struct kunit *test)
+{
+	const u64 v = RIDE_VBLANK, t0 = 1000 * RIDE_MS;
+
+	/* No client present and no brightness-only present yet: send now. */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(t0, 0, 0, 0, v), 0ULL);
+	/* No vblank known: never hold a level back. */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(t0, t0, v, t0, 0), 0ULL);
+
+	/* A 120 Hz client: its next present is due within 1.5 vblanks. */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(t0 + RIDE_MS, t0, v, 0, v),
+			v + v / 2 - RIDE_MS);
+	/* The first present after a pause counts one vblank. */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(t0, t0, 0, 0, v), v + v / 2);
+	/* A 60 Hz client on the 120 Hz panel: two vblanks and a half. */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(t0 + RIDE_MS, t0, 2 * v, 0, v),
+			2 * v + v / 2 - RIDE_MS);
+	/* A slower client is bounded to two vblanks: a 30 Hz gap is free. */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(t0 + 25 * RIDE_MS, t0, 4 * v, 0, v),
+			0ULL);
+	/* The client stopped: no frame is due, send now. */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(t0 + 13 * RIDE_MS, t0, v, 0, v),
+			0ULL);
+
+	/* At most one brightness-only present per vblank, flips or not. */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(t0 + 3 * RIDE_MS, 0, 0, t0, v),
+			v - 3 * RIDE_MS);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(t0 + v, 0, 0, t0, v), 0ULL);
+	/* Both bounds: the later one wins. */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(t0 + RIDE_MS, t0, v, t0, v),
+			v + v / 2 - RIDE_MS);
+}
+
+/*
+ * A fade under a 120 Hz client: each step is carried by the next client
+ * present, no step needs a brightness-only present, and the fade ends at
+ * its target at the same time as without the client.
+ */
+static void backlight_ride_fade_test(struct kunit *test)
+{
+	struct dcp_backlight_state state;
+	struct dcp_backlight_present present;
+	const u64 v = RIDE_VBLANK;
+	u64 now, last_flip = 0, interval = 0, start = 1000 * RIDE_MS;
+	unsigned int carried = 0, own = 0, step = 0;
+	u32 prev;
+
+	KUNIT_ASSERT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_init(&state, 600, true, 186, false, 0), 0);
+	state.fade = true;
+	KUNIT_ASSERT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_request(&state, 246, false, false), 0);
+	KUNIT_ASSERT_TRUE(test, state.fading);
+	prev = state.actual;
+
+	/* 1 ms ticks for 400 ms: steps every 16 ms, client presents every vblank. */
+	for (now = start; now < start + 400 * RIDE_MS; now += RIDE_MS) {
+		u32 elapsed = div_u64(now - start, RIDE_MS);
+
+		if (elapsed % 16 == 0)
+			dcp_bl_fade_step(&state, elapsed, 250);
+		/* The worker, kicked by a dirty step, asks whether it may send. */
+		if (state.dirty && !state.in_flight &&
+		    !dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(now, last_flip, interval, 0, v)) {
+			KUNIT_ASSERT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_prepare(&state, true, &present), 0);
+			KUNIT_ASSERT_TRUE(test, dcp_bl_complete(&state, present.sequence, true));
+			own++;
+		}
+		/* A client present on each vblank boundary carries any pending level. */
+		if (now - start >= (u64)step * v) {
+			int ret = dcp_bl_prepare(&state, true, &present);
+
+			if (!ret) {
+				KUNIT_ASSERT_TRUE(test, dcp_bl_complete(&state, present.sequence,
+									true));
+				carried++;
+			} else {
+				KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, ret, -EALREADY);
+			}
+			/* Monotonic up to the target, never past it. */
+			KUNIT_EXPECT_GE(test, state.actual, prev);
+			KUNIT_EXPECT_LE(test, state.actual, 246U);
+			prev = state.actual;
+			if (last_flip)
+				interval = now - last_flip;
+			last_flip = now;
+			step++;
+		}
+	}
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, own, 0U);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_GE(test, carried, 12U);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, state.fading);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, state.dirty);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, state.actual, 246U);
+}
+
+/*
+ * The same fade with no client presents: every step goes out on its own,
+ * one per vblank at most, and the target is presented when the fade's clock
+ * ends, within the 300 ms the W6 r5 gate allows.
+ */
+static void backlight_ride_idle_fade_test(struct kunit *test)
+{
+	struct dcp_backlight_state state;
+	struct dcp_backlight_present present;
+	const u64 v = RIDE_VBLANK;
+	u64 now, last_swap = 0, start = 1000 * RIDE_MS, done = 0;
+	unsigned int own = 0;
+
+	KUNIT_ASSERT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_init(&state, 600, true, 246, false, 0), 0);
+	state.fade = true;
+	KUNIT_ASSERT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_request(&state, 186, false, false), 0);
+
+	for (now = start; now < start + 400 * RIDE_MS; now += RIDE_MS) {
+		u32 elapsed = div_u64(now - start, RIDE_MS);
+
+		if (elapsed % 16 == 0)
+			dcp_bl_fade_step(&state, elapsed, 250);
+		if (state.dirty && !state.in_flight &&
+		    !dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(now, 0, 0, last_swap, v)) {
+			if (last_swap)
+				KUNIT_EXPECT_GE(test, now - last_swap, v);
+			KUNIT_ASSERT_EQ(test, dcp_bl_prepare(&state, true, &present), 0);
+			KUNIT_ASSERT_TRUE(test, dcp_bl_complete(&state, present.sequence, true));
+			last_swap = now;
+			own++;
+			if (state.actual == 186U && !done)
+				done = now - start;
+		}
+	}
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_GE(test, own, 12U);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, state.actual, 186U);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_GE(test, done, 250 * RIDE_MS);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_LT(test, done, 300 * RIDE_MS);
+}
+
 static struct kunit_case backlight_cases[] = {
 	KUNIT_CASE(backlight_reports_keep_target_test),
 	KUNIT_CASE(backlight_millinits_takeover_test),
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index fcd8b93a4d..a84ed1de82 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -208,7 +208,7 @@ struct iomfb_m4 {
 	size_t coproc_size;
 	/* The realtime bandwidth mailbox from the DT (0: none), see dcp_m4_bw_mailbox() */
 	u64 bw_mailbox;
-	struct work_struct backlight_work;
+	struct delayed_work backlight_work;
 	void __iomem *coproc;
 	struct apple_rtkit *rtkit;
 	struct mutex lock;
@@ -247,6 +247,15 @@ struct iomfb_m4 {
 	struct drm_framebuffer *uncertain_fb;
 	struct dcp_m4_frame active_frame;
 	u64 flips, blanks, brightness_swaps;
+	/*
+	 * Fade steps ride on client presents (dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns()): the last
+	 * client present and the interval before it, the last brightness-only
+	 * present (ktime ns), the client presents that carried a new level, the
+	 * brightness-only presents put off, and whether the last swap carried one.
+	 */
+	u64 last_flip_ns, flip_interval_ns, last_brightness_ns;
+	u64 brightness_carried, brightness_deferred;
+	bool swap_carried;
 	/* The ADT panel properties, read once by iomfb_m4_panel_edid(). */
 	bool panel_adt_read, panel_p3;
 	u32 panel_edr_headroom; /* 16.16, 0 if the ADT has none */
@@ -2863,7 +2872,7 @@ int iomfb_m4_init(struct apple_dcp *owner)
 	mutex_init(&dcp->ext_modes_lock);
 	spin_lock_init(&dcp->state_lock);
 	init_completion(&dcp->reply);
-	INIT_WORK(&dcp->backlight_work, iomfb_m4_backlight_work);
+	INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&dcp->backlight_work, iomfb_m4_backlight_work);
 	spin_lock_init(&dcp->ext_put_lock);
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&dcp->ext_puts);
 	INIT_WORK(&dcp->ext_put_work, iomfb_m4_ext_put_work);
@@ -3810,6 +3819,7 @@ static int iomfb_m4_swap(struct iomfb_m4 *dcp, const struct dcp_m4_frame *frame)
 	dcp->runtime->level = 0;
 	if (!prepared)
 		dcp_backlight_complete(dcp->owner, present.sequence, !ret);
+	dcp->swap_carried = !prepared && !ret;
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -3819,6 +3829,7 @@ int iomfb_m4_present(struct apple_dcp *owner, struct drm_framebuffer *fb,
 	struct iomfb_m4 *dcp = owner->v26_6;
 	struct drm_framebuffer *retire = NULL;
 	struct dcp_m4_frame frame;
+	u64 now;
 	int ret;
 
 	if (!dcp || !dcp->runtime || !fb || fb->format->num_planes != 1 ||
@@ -3869,6 +3880,13 @@ int iomfb_m4_present(struct apple_dcp *owner, struct drm_framebuffer *fb,
 	dcp->active_fb = fb;
 	dcp->active_frame = frame;
 	dcp->flips++;
+	if (dcp->swap_carried)
+		dcp->brightness_carried++;
+	/* The client's cadence: its next present will carry a pending level. */
+	now = ktime_get_ns();
+	if (dcp->last_flip_ns)
+		dcp->flip_interval_ns = now - dcp->last_flip_ns;
+	dcp->last_flip_ns = now;
 	iomfb_m4_idle_cache_kick(dcp);
 out:
 	mutex_unlock(&dcp->lock);
@@ -5839,9 +5857,27 @@ int iomfb_m4_resume(struct apple_dcp *owner)
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/* One vblank of the running mode in ns; 120 Hz until the timing is known. */
+static u64 iomfb_m4_vblank_ns(struct iomfb_m4 *dcp)
+{
+	u32 rate = dcp->runtime ? dcp->runtime->timing.refresh_16_16 : 0;
+
+	if (rate < (24U << 16) || rate > (240U << 16))
+		return div_u64(NSEC_PER_SEC, 120);
+	return div_u64((u64)NSEC_PER_SEC << 16, rate);
+}
+
+/*
+ * A pending level goes out on the next client present while the client
+ * flips; only once none is due does it take a brightness-only present of
+ * its own, so a fade does not take swap slots from the client.  The fade's
+ * clock and levels are those of dcp_backlight.c; this only picks the present.
+ */
 static void iomfb_m4_backlight_work(struct work_struct *work)
 {
-	struct iomfb_m4 *dcp = container_of(work, struct iomfb_m4, backlight_work);
+	struct iomfb_m4 *dcp = container_of(to_delayed_work(work), struct iomfb_m4,
+					    backlight_work);
+	u64 wait;
 	int ret;
 
 	mutex_lock(&dcp->lock);
@@ -5849,12 +5885,25 @@ static void iomfb_m4_backlight_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	    !dcp_backlight_pending(dcp->owner) || !dcp->active_frame.dva)
 		goto out;
 	ret = dcp_m4_runtime_live(dcp->runtime);
-	if (!ret)
+	if (!ret) {
+		wait = dcp_bl_ride_wait_ns(ktime_get_ns(), dcp->last_flip_ns,
+					   dcp->flip_interval_ns,
+					   dcp->last_brightness_ns,
+					   iomfb_m4_vblank_ns(dcp));
+		if (wait) {
+			/* Looked at again then; a client present may carry it first. */
+			dcp->brightness_deferred++;
+			queue_delayed_work(dcp->runtime->wq, &dcp->backlight_work,
+					   usecs_to_jiffies(div_u64(wait, NSEC_PER_USEC) + 1));
+			goto out;
+		}
 		ret = iomfb_m4_swap(dcp, &dcp->active_frame);
+	}
 	if (ret) {
 		dcp_m4_failed(dcp, ret);
 	} else {
 		dcp->brightness_swaps++;
+		dcp->last_brightness_ns = ktime_get_ns();
 		iomfb_m4_idle_cache_kick(dcp);
 	}
 out:
@@ -5865,8 +5914,9 @@ static void iomfb_m4_backlight_kick(struct apple_dcp *owner)
 {
 	struct iomfb_m4 *dcp = owner->v26_6;
 
+	/* A put-off present stays put off: it is looked at again in time. */
 	if (dcp && dcp->runtime && !READ_ONCE(owner->quiescing))
-		queue_work(dcp->runtime->wq, &dcp->backlight_work);
+		queue_delayed_work(dcp->runtime->wq, &dcp->backlight_work, 0);
 }
 
 void iomfb_m4_configure_backlight(struct apple_dcp *owner)
@@ -5890,7 +5940,7 @@ void iomfb_m4_quiesce(struct apple_dcp *owner)
 		return;
 	/* Wake any RPC waiter before waiting for workers; never recycle its DMA. */
 	dcp_m4_failed(dcp, -ENODEV);
-	cancel_work_sync(&dcp->backlight_work);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&dcp->backlight_work);
 	if (dcp->runtime)
 		flush_workqueue(dcp->runtime->wq);
 	/* After the flush, as drained callbacks can queue it. */
@@ -5925,6 +5975,9 @@ static int iomfb_m4_status_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
 	seq_printf(s, "flips=%llu blanks=%llu backlight_swaps=%llu active=%u uncertain=%u\n",
 		   dcp->flips, dcp->blanks, dcp->brightness_swaps,
 		   !!dcp->active_fb, !!dcp->uncertain_fb);
+	seq_printf(s, "backlight_carried=%llu backlight_deferred=%llu vblank_us=%llu\n",
+		   dcp->brightness_carried, dcp->brightness_deferred,
+		   div_u64(iomfb_m4_vblank_ns(dcp), NSEC_PER_USEC));
 	seq_printf(s, "display_off=%u off_cycles=%llu off_us=%lld/%lld on_us=%lld/%lld\n",
 		   dcp->display_off, dcp->display_off_cycles,
 		   dcp->display_off_us, dcp->display_off_us_max,
